"Both pundits converge on a Czech Republic win. CZE Pundit predicts 2-0; RSA Pundit concedes ground after rebuttal and lands on 2-1 CZE. The decisive factor cited by both is the double midfield suspension for South Africa (Sithole and Zwane, both red-carded vs Mexico), which leaves Bafana rebuilding their entire central structure. Schick and Hlozek identified as the primary threats; Ronwen Williams and Iqraam Rayners cited as RSA's best hope of a consolation."